# Session Start - READ LEARNINGS FIRST

**BEFORE doing ANY work on Rift, you MUST:**

1. Read `.cursor/rules/project-structure.mdc` — repo layout, remotes, critical rules
2. Read `.cursor/rules/agent-autonomy.mdc` — learnings and known bugs
3. Pay special attention to "Learnings from" sections at the end of agent-autonomy.mdc
4. Note which bugs have already been fixed so you don't re-discover them

**Key learnings to remember:**
- Two remotes: `origin` = private `mkmk10k/rift-dev`, `public` = open-source `mkmk10k/rift`
- NEVER push directly to `public` remote — use `bun run publish-public`
- TTS/STT must use bundled Python, not system Python
- `prompts.json` must NOT be gitignored (it is needed at runtime)
- Use `pip show` not `import` for diagnostics (Metal GPU crash)
- Version comparison needs hash check for same-day releases
- Website lives at `website/` inside this repo, not in a separate folder

**At session END, update `agent-autonomy.mdc` with new learnings.**

If you skip reading learnings, you WILL waste time re-fixing known bugs.
